 they're Prosthetics is because we know  that morphid Clark who plays Galadriel  isn't an actual elf though she is pretty  convincing in this role Clark says  there's an amazing  Prosthetics artist Irina painting them  day and night and says that they were  even painting tiny veins on the ears all  that attention to detail definitely paid  off  number eight it was important to make  the Orcs look realistic as well as bit  with the rest of tolkien's lore all  while allowing the actors who played  them to actually fight as a result the  Orcs Prosthetics were designed to let  them move easily they also have extra  lines scars and wrinkles on their skin  to show the Orcs pasts number nine it  took quite a lot of effort to make the  heart foots look like heart foots as  well sever zangabani plays the hard foot  Marigold Brandy foot and she said that  she was excited to get her costume until  she realized she'd be wearing huge feet  and getting covered in mud she joked  that this was a bit of a come down she  went on to explain that those feet made  things pretty difficult at first but in  her words we had this incredible team of  people who kept refining them and by the  end they became part of us and we didn't  want to take them off number 10 after  seeing all those amazing costumes it's  very clear that cosplayers are going to  be super excited about recreating looks  from the rings of power in reality  though this actually had a little  something to do with the actual costume  design process the costume designer Kate  Hawley set out to make sure that the  inevitable cosplayers would struggle to  replicate her intricate designs and it's  safe to say she did a good job it'll  take a pretty dedicated cosplayer to  make a 16-piece beard but we're sure  somebody at Comic-Con will make it  happen number 11. the Orcs in particular  are pretty amazing to look at and it's  wild to think that creatures like that  aren't actually real Morphin Clark  agrees and says that even though they  know that the Orcs aren't actually real  it's still scary to see them running  towards you yeah that's completely Fair  she does say though they're uniquely  unfightening when they're drinking a  smoothie in between takes Orcs they're  just like us  number 12. so how did those Orcs look so  convincing the Orcs facial Prosthetics  were made from something called  encapsulated silicon this is two layers  of silicon that have a piece of silicon  between them that can move this way they  can move their faces with ease this  means that the new Orcs look a lot more  realistic than those from The Lord of  the Rings The Fellowship of the Ring  back in 2001 according to Jamie Wilson  the head of the prosthetic Department of  the race of power the new materials work  with the actors moving with their skin  and reaching the same temperature as the  actor's skin growing transparent making  the application of the intense orc  makeup that much simpler number 13 wigs  for fantasy series can be a difficult  thing to make look realistic internet  backlash towards a certain other current  fantasy show has proven that to be true  but we aren't naming any names the rings  of power characters on the other hand  have some very convincing hair a core  according to Sophia nombetti her hair  and costumes were what made her  character come alive she added that her  wig garnered the nickname Gloria number  14. with all the work money attention to  detail and incredible amounts of  patience required to make these  characters come to life via costumes and  makeup it's easy to wonder why put the  actors through all of this when it could  all be added in Via CGI well Jamie  Wilson says that it was extremely  important to the folks making this  series that it was all real as possible  in his words there are hundreds of  Productions that are heavy on visual  effects and you can see it that the  human eye is getting better and better  and knows what is real and knows what  isn't number 15 